  "home.faqHeading": "Frequently asked questions",
  "home.faq.what.q": "What is Aion DPS?",
  "home.faq.what.a": "Aion DPS (aiondps.com), short for Daevas Power Suite, is a free, open-source companion app for AION 2. It shows live combat stats for your whole group and brings boss leaderboards, character profiles, an interactive map and event and world boss timers, using passive packet capture.",
  "home.faq.stand.q": "What does DPS stand for?",
  "home.faq.stand.a": "Daevas Power Suite. The name comes from the world of damage-per-second meters, where Aion DPS started, and grew into a full toolkit for AION 2.",
  "home.faq.safe.q": "Is Aion DPS allowed?",
  "home.faq.safe.a": "NCSOFT names no individual programs, only sanctioned behaviors such as bots or tools that raise damage. Aion DPS only reads the network traffic your own computer already receives; it never reads game memory, injects code or sends game data to the game (only if you yourself switch on the network tool does it ping the game server). That it falls outside those rules is our reading, not a statement from NCSOFT, so check the current rules and use it at your own risk.",
  "home.faq.install.q": "How do I install Aion DPS?",
  "home.faq.install.a": "Install the Npcap driver, download the Windows installer from aiondps.com/download, and start AION 2. Aion DPS picks up your fights automatically and updates itself.",
  "home.faq.free.q": "Is Aion DPS free?",
  "home.faq.free.a": "Yes. It is free and open source under the MIT license, and uploads to the boss leaderboards are optional and off by default.",
