  "legal.termsTitle": "Terms of Service",
  "legal.termsIntro": "These Terms of Service apply to the Aion DPS desktop client and the aiondps.com website (also reachable as daevasuite.com and daevaspowersuite.com). By using either, you agree to the points below.",
  "legal.termsSection1Heading": "Acceptance of Terms",
  "legal.termsSection1Body": "By downloading the client or using this website, you agree to these Terms of Service. If you do not agree, please do not use the client or upload data to the site.",
  "legal.termsSection2Heading": "A Fan-Made Community Project",
  "legal.termsSection2Body": "Aion DPS is an independent, fan-made project built by and for the Aion community. It is not affiliated with, endorsed by, or associated with NCSoft or any other publisher of the Aion games.",
  "legal.termsSection3Heading": "Free of Charge, Provided \"As Is\"",
  "legal.termsSection3Body": "The client and website are provided free of charge, with no warranty of any kind, express or implied. We do not guarantee the tool will be error-free, accurate, or available at all times.",
  "legal.termsSection4Heading": "Your Responsibility for Game Rules",
  "legal.termsSection4Body":
    "The client reads your own computer's network traffic passively. It never modifies the game client, injects code, or sends any game packets. The only thing it sends towards the game server is an ordinary ping (one tiny echo request per second, without any game content), and only if you yourself switch on the network overlay or open the network page, and only while it is on; the same ping goes to your router and to 1.1.1.1. Even so, some games restrict the use of third-party tools, so it is your responsibility to check the current terms of service of the game you are playing before using this or any similar tool. NCSOFT's current rules: [Operating policy](https://aion2.plaync.com/de-de/board/rules/list) and [Terms of Service](https://www.plaync.com/policy/service/game_de). The pet overlay also reads a small area of the screen (the target plate); the picture stays in memory and is never saved or sent.",
  "legal.termsSection5Heading": "How the Upload Feature Works",
  "legal.termsSection5Body": "Uploading is optional and only sends the combat data described in our Privacy Policy. We reserve the right to reject, remove, or hide any upload without notice.",
  "legal.termsSection6Heading": "Acceptable Use",
  "legal.termsSection6Body": "The upload feature is meant for real gameplay data only. Uploading fabricated, manipulated, or spam data to the leaderboards is not allowed, and we may block characters or IP hashes that do this.",
  "legal.termsSection7Heading": "Availability and Changes",
  "legal.termsSection7Body": "This is a hobby project maintained in our spare time. Features, leaderboards, or the service as a whole may change, be temporarily unavailable, or be discontinued at any time without notice.",
  "legal.termsSection8Heading": "Open Source",
  "legal.termsSection8Body": "The project's source code is publicly available on GitHub under an open-source license. You are welcome to review it, report issues, or contribute, but you may not use it to impersonate the official project or claim it as your own.",
  "legal.termsSection9Heading": "Limitation of Liability",
  "legal.termsSection9Body": "To the fullest extent permitted by law, we are not liable for any damages, losses, or issues, including any in-game consequences, arising from your use of the client or website. You use this tool entirely at your own risk.",
  "legal.termsSection10Heading": "Governing Law",
  "legal.termsSection10Body": "These Terms are governed by the laws applicable at the operator's place of business in Germany, to the extent permitted by law.",
  "legal.termsSection11Heading": "Contact",
  "legal.termsSection11Body": "Questions about these Terms can be asked on the Discord community server linked on the site, or by opening an issue on the project's GitHub page.",
