  "download.heroDescription":
    "A companion app for Aion 2 with live combat stats that passively observes your own computer's network traffic - never the game's memory, no interference with the game. Runs alongside the game as its own window or as a transparent overlay.",
  "download.feature1Title": "Live damage & healing",
  "download.feature1Text":
    "Shows DPS/HPS per player in real time, including a skill breakdown - read from the network traffic your own client already produces.",
  "download.feature2Title": "Transparent overlay",
  "download.feature2Text":
    "One click switches to a click-through overlay mode that sits on top of the game without getting in the way.",
  "download.feature3Title": "Community leaderboards (optional)",
  "download.feature3Text":
    "You can upload boss fights and compare yourself with others. If you switch it on in the settings, your own character profile is uploaded automatically after you log in (off by default) so that you can be found on this site.",
  "download.feature4Title": "Stays local",
  "download.feature4Text":
    "Without an upload, no data about you leaves your computer apart from the update check and the requests listed in the privacy policy - Aion DPS reads the network traffic that your own client already produces.",
  "download.installationHeading": "Installation",
  "download.step1": "Download and run the installer (the installer needs no admin rights and installs per user).",
  "download.step2":
    "Install the Npcap driver from npcap.com (Aion DPS reads the game's network traffic through it) - it is not part of the installer.",
  "download.step3":
    "Start Aion DPS, then log in with your character: it reads your character, gear and skills from the game itself.",
  "download.step4":
    "Your character's server is detected automatically. If you switch on the profile upload in the settings (off by default), your profile is uploaded after login - that is how you become findable on this site.",
  "download.step5": "Done - Aion DPS updates itself automatically after that, whenever a new version is released.",
  "download.requirementsHeading": "Requirements",
  "download.requirementsText": "Windows 10 or 11 and the Npcap driver, which Aion DPS uses to see the game's network traffic. Npcap is not part of the installer.",
  "download.screenshotsHeading": "Screenshots",
  "download.faqHeading": "Frequently asked questions",
  "download.faq1Q": "Is it allowed to use?",
  "download.faq1A": "NCSOFT does not name individual programs; it lists behaviors that are sanctioned: bypassing technical protection, bots, tools that raise damage or speed, anything that lets players do what regular players cannot. Aion DPS does none of that: it only reads the network traffic your own computer already receives, through the Npcap driver, and never reads game memory, injects code, hooks the game client or sends game data to the game (only if you yourself switch on the network tool does it ping the game server). Damage meters are not prohibited by those rules, but not expressly approved either, and the list is not exhaustive. That Aion DPS falls outside it is our reading, not a statement from NCSOFT, so check the current rules and use it at your own responsibility.",
  "download.faq2Q": "Does it cost anything?",
  "download.faq2A": "No. Aion DPS is free and open source under the MIT license.",
  "download.faq3Q": "Which AION 2 regions does it support?",
  "download.faq3A": "The global release of AION 2, every region NCSOFT launched on 5 October 2026. Korea and Taiwan run a few versions ahead, so skill recognition may be incomplete there.",
  "download.faq4Q": "Do I need administrator rights?",
  "download.faq4A": "Not for the installer: Aion DPS installs per user and updates itself without them. The meter itself asks for them at every start (a UAC prompt), because it needs them for the packet capture and for its overlays over the game. The installer of the Npcap driver asks for them as well.",
  "download.faq5Q": "Are my fights uploaded automatically?",
  "download.faq5A": "No. Uploads to the leaderboards are off by default and you decide in the settings whether to switch them on.",
  "download.repoLinkPrefix": "Source code, README and changelog: ",
  "download.vtNote": "Every installer is scanned with VirusTotal before it is published; the report is linked in the notes of each release.",
  "download.vtLink": "Latest release and its VirusTotal report",
