  "guide.c.extrasShugo": "Checklist, pet radar, threat meter, PvP frames, map and timers, training dummy, build detection; the website adds an armory, tier list, database (items, skills, quests, crafting), news and patch notes, and a stream list with Drops",
  "guide.c.rankShugo": "Combat power leaderboard (the game's own score); no fight uploads or DPS leaderboards mentioned",
  "guide.c.closedAbyss": "Not published (its GitHub page holds only the README and images)",
  "guide.c.priceAbyss": "Free; supporters on Ko-fi get more fight storage (50 GB instead of 2 GB)",
  "guide.c.regionsAbyss": "Six: TW, KR, NA, SA, EU, Asia",
  "guide.c.overlayAbyss": "Yes – DPS bars, boss card with HP and berserk timer, compact strip, hides when idle",
  "guide.c.skillsAbyss": "Yes – crit, back, parry and multi-hit rates, skill and buff timelines against boss HP",
  "guide.c.cooldownAbyss": "Yes – cooldowns, buffs and debuffs as bars with class presets and sounds",
  "guide.c.historyAbyss": "Yes – fights kept on your PC, dungeon runs grouped; on the web public, unlisted or private",
  "guide.c.rankAbyss": "Leaderboards per region and boss, class statistics by combat power bracket, on abysslogs.com",
  "guide.c.extrasAbyss": "Dungeon lobby with gear score and combat power, event and boss timers, training dummy parse capping, ticket tracker, ping and FPS display, hotkeys to hide the overlay and reset the fight",
  "guide.lago": "LagoFast is a game booster that ships a DPS tracker inside its own app. It is the only option here that also optimizes your connection to the game. Our network overlay measures ping, jitter and packet loss but changes nothing.",
  "guide.rdpsWhy": "Why we have no rDPS: rDPS estimates how much of a player's damage comes from other players' buffs and moves that share to whoever set the buff. It rests on modelling assumptions (how buffs stack, how strong they are, whether the damage was useful) and not on measured numbers. We show measured damage and fight time instead.",
  "guide.also": "Also worth knowing: since the patch of 1 April 2026 the game has a combat analysis of its own, which shows only your own damage and needs no extra program. AION2 Hub is a fan site that promotes the AionFlex meter (compared above) rather than a separate meter. Several more free projects exist (for example Eclipse, Wingbeat and Aion2-QoL; not all of them are open source) and forks of the projects above, which we did not compare one by one.",
  "guide.h.weak": "Where we are weaker",
  "guide.weak.stars": "Several projects have far more GitHub stars than we do. We are young and little known.",
  "guide.weak.regions": "Korea and Taiwan are only partly supported: those servers run a few versions ahead, so skill recognition is incomplete there. Other meters cover them fully.",
  "guide.weak.platform": "Windows only. There is no Linux or Proton version.",
  "guide.weak.driver": "The Npcap driver has to be installed separately. One other meter bundles its own driver.",
  "guide.weak.missing": "We have no rDPS (the figure that credits a player's damage to whoever set the buff), no character scorer and no connection optimization like LagoFast's. We chose iDPS on purpose: it counts only measured damage over the fight time, while rDPS rests on assumptions about how buffs stack, because the game's damage formula is not published. The price is that a support's value shows in the group's kill time, not in their own number.",
  "guide.weak.boards": "The leaderboards come only from fights that players uploaded, and the group of uploaders is still small next to the large meters. Over 30,000 fights are in so far.",
  "guide.weak.estimates": "Some figures are estimates: the cooldown times in the Assist window are calculated from each skill's speed and are off by about 16 % on average, and the Expert mode of the stat calculator is still a beta.",
  "guide.h.strong": "Where we are stronger",
  "guide.strong.analyzer": "The combat analyzer with deaths, replay and a plausibility check of the boss damage against the hit points it really lost.",
  "guide.strong.oneTool": "Map, pets, gathering spots, event timetable, world boss timers, a crafting calculator, a network report, a dashboard with widgets, an overlay designer, a design editor, a statistics page and a daily checklist in the same program.",
  "guide.strong.boards": "Boss leaderboards and character profiles on aiondps.com with optional upload.",
  "guide.strong.update": "Automatic updates without admin rights.",
  "guide.h.oss": "Why open source matters for a damage meter",
  "guide.oss.check": "You can check it yourself. A meter sees your network traffic. With open source anyone can read what it does and what it sends. Here that is no game data to the game (only if you yourself switch on the network tool does it ping the game server), and uploads are off by default.",
  "guide.oss.lockin": "No lock-in. If a project stops, the code stays. Anyone can fork it or fix it after a game patch.",
  "guide.oss.paywall": "No paywalled basics. Free software has no tier that hides your own group's numbers.",
  "guide.oss.fixes": "Fixes in public. Bugs and new skills can be reported and fixed openly, and every release is documented in the changelog.",
  "guide.oss.licenses": "Licenses differ. The MIT license of this meter allows any use, including closed forks. The GPL projects require derived work to stay open. Both are open source.",
  "guide.h.faq": "Questions",
  "guide.faq.tracker.q": "Is it also an AION 2 combat tracker?",
  "guide.faq.tracker.a": "Yes. It records every fight with the skills used, damage, healing, deaths and a replay, so you can review a fight afterwards.",
  "guide.installShort": "The meter installs in three steps: the Npcap driver, the installer and your login. The installer and updates need no administrator rights; the meter itself asks for them at every start. The steps are on the download page.",
  "guide.faq.choose.q": "Which AION 2 DPS meter should I choose?",
  "guide.faq.choose.a": "That depends on what you need. Use the tables: your region (some meters cover Korea and Taiwan fully, ours only partly), your platform (Windows or Linux), the extras you want (map, timers, leaderboards, rotation view, rDPS) and whether you want the source code to be open. Whatever you pick, check what it does with your data.",
  "guide.faq.rdps.q": "Why does the meter not show rDPS?",
  "guide.faq.rdps.a": "rDPS estimates how much of a player's damage comes from other players' buffs and moves that share to whoever set the buff. That rests on modelling assumptions, not on measured numbers. We show the iDPS per target and the fight time instead, which show the effect of a buff on the group without estimating anything.",
